<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base up 0.48 pct in Oct 25 week.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base up 0.48 pct in Oct 25 week.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base grew 0.48 percent to 2.74 billion sucres in the week to October 25, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In September, money base grew 0.87 percent to 2.56 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The bank did not give any reason for the increase.</p>
<p>In the previous week, monetary base fell 2.15 percent.</p>
<p>The money base ended 1995 at 2.41 billion sucres, up from 1.85 billion sucres at the end of 1994.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
